<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency bought 100,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian wheat, 40,000 of Canadian barley and 20,000 of Australian barley, all for May shipment, an agency official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the purchases (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY   QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	100,000	Dark Northern Spring   60,000</p>
<p>				Hard Red Winter	  20,000</p>
<p>				(protein 13.0 percent)</p>
<p>				Hard Red Winter</p>
<p>			     (protein 11.5 percent)  20,000</p>
<p> Canada     20,000	Western Red Spring     20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	Feed			 40,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk, +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
